    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that the costs are coming down, but it feels like you're dismissing a lot of the actual economic fallout for the people and industries currently reliant on the old system. if the transition is basically a done deal and \"inevitable\" as you say, does that mean the concerns about energy poverty or the economic instability of fossil fuel-dependent regions are basically just irrelevant or outdated?",
